function info(kind){if(mode==='demo')stopDemo();const privacy=kind==='privacy';$('#info-title').textContent=privacy?'Small footprint. Clear limits.':'Your attention, with a little help.';$('#info-body').innerHTML=privacy?`<div class="info-grid"><div class="info-item"><strong>Your text</strong><p>Local mode processes text in this tab. It is not uploaded, saved to an account, or sent to an AI service. Pinned sentences disappear on reload. Hosting access logs may still record a normal page visit.</p></div><div class="info-item"><strong>Your camera</strong><p>Camera access is optional. After you consent, the browser loads a pinned copy of WebGazer and its face model assets from this website. The website host receives ordinary asset requests. Camera frames and gaze coordinates are processed in your browser, with no recording or gaze export by Skim. Stop or switch to Pointer to release the camera.</p></div><div class="info-item"><strong>What the lens cannot tell you</strong><p>It does not know what you understand, prove that a claim is true, or reliably locate an exact word. A calibration score is a short sample, not an ongoing accuracy guarantee.</p></div><div class="info-item"><strong>Optional Jev</strong><p>The downloadable local server supports Jev when you provide your own server-side API key. Enabling it sends the current paragraph, goal, and focus words to TypeSafe. No webcam frames are sent. The hosted demo uses local selection.</p></div></div>`:`<div class="info-grid"><div class="info-item"><strong>1. Point, look, or use your keyboard</strong><p>Pointer mode is ready immediately. Webcam mode is an experiment: calibrate, pass an independent accuracy check, and keep your head steady. Arrow keys move through paragraphs.</p></div><div class="info-item"><strong>2. Tell the lens what matters</strong><p>Choose the answer, next steps, a catch, or key details. Add a focus word if you are hunting for something specific. Sentence selection changes with that goal.</p></div><div class="info-item"><strong>3. Keep the original context</strong><p>The lens emphasizes one exact sentence in the active paragraph. It never rewrites the source or moves the words. Pin up to five sentences or turn off emphasis to compare.</p></div><p class="measure-note">The demo tour uses simulated attention. The webcam path uses real estimates, but human accuracy has not been validated for your camera. No speed or comprehension improvement is claimed.</p></div>`;$('#info-dialog').showModal();}
